It is possible to use a modified font in both modes - full screen and 
windowed. Here we routinely use an old DOS program that changes the VGA 
fonts on the graphics adapter, so cyrillic symbols can be displayed 
correctly. This works flawlessly in full-screen text mode under NT and 
2000, which probably means under all other kinds of Windows.
The other possibility is to create a custom TrueType font for use in 
windowed text mode. 
I don't know how to do either. If you wish, I could look at home for an 
